"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Verisk Analytics, Inc. engages in the provision of data analytics and technology solutions to the insurance industry in the United States and internationally. The company offers underwriting solutions, including forms, rules, and loss costs services that provides policy language, prospective loss costs, policy writing and rating rules, and underwriting solutions for risk selection and segmentation, pricing, and workflow optimization; underwriting data and analytics solutions, which provides property and auto specific rating, and underwriting information solutions; catastrophe modelling and risk solutions; life insurance solutions for transforming current workflows in life insurance underwriting, claim insights, policy administration, unclaimed property/equity, compliance and fraud detection, and actuarial and portfolio modelling; specialty business solutions, which provides full end-to-end management of insurance and reinsurance business; and international underwriting solutions. It also provides claims insurance solutions, including property estimating solutions, provide data, analytics, and networking solutions for professionals involved in estimating all phases of building repair and reconstruction; anti-fraud solutions that provide fraud-detection tools for the property and casualty insurance industry; casualty solutions, which focus on compliance, casualty claims decision, and workflow automation; and international claims solutions, which focus on personal injury and motor franchises with complementary offerings to the property claims solutions. The company was founded in 1971 and is headquartered in Jersey City, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Lee M. Shavel | CEO, President & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $384K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $149K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Verisk Analytics, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $25.9B market cap on $3.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 21% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $1.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 39 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.58\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 7.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Carries a 51% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5127164924325169},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 15% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 35% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trillium Asset Management LLC Sells 2,810 Shares of Verisk Analytics, Inc. $VRSK","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/15/trillium-asset-management-llc-sells-2810-shares-of-verisk-analytics-inc-vrsk.html","date":"2026-11-15","timestamp":1794775741.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.949,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Verisk Analytics, Inc. $VRSK Stock: Mawer Investment Management Ltd. Raises Stake","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/15/verisk-analytics-inc-vrsk-stock-mawer-investment-management-ltd-raises-stake.html","date":"2026-11-15","timestamp":1794772116.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.912,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (VRSK) Volat